A glob view prints a YAML file's header comment, or else a field summary of its first three scalar keys, with `...` when more follow; a file with only mappings and lists has nothing to summarize.
Expected output is hand-written: the TypeScript build has no data file support.
== args
input
== file input/commented.yaml
# Commented settings.
a: 1
== file input/compose.yml
version: "3"
services:
  web: {}
name: demo
== file input/many.yaml
a: 1
b: two
c: true
d: null
== file input/nested.yaml
a:
  b: 1
== stdout
glob view: input
Includes only a header or summary per file.
For file-level outlines, use `outln [FILE]...`.
input/commented.yaml: Commented settings.
input/compose.yml: {version: "3", name: demo}
input/many.yaml: {a: 1, b: two, c: true, ...}
input/nested.yaml: (no header available)
== stderr
== exit 0
